      "prompt": "Continue directly from the final visible state of the accepted preceding shot in the same dawn-lit stone-paved courtyard threshold. Keep the same fixed barred gate, with Vikramaditya on frame left facing screen right and Vetala on frame right behind the bars; preserve their established identities, spacing, eyeline, camera axis, and natural screen direction. Begin from their accepted end-state: Vikramaditya is standing still and listening; Vetala raises one hand visibly between the bars and begins answering the still-unresolved riddle. Keep the action small, clear, and physically plausible. Maintain the same early-dawn light and restrained live-action historical Indian visual grounding. A modestly tighter composition may leave the incidental foreground lantern and padlock out of frame; do not make them story objects. Keep the gate and stone threshold continuous. Do not return to the banyan road, imply a time or location jump, open or remove the gate, release Vetala, add a character, prop, location, or story event, introduce magic, or resolve the riddle. No captions, logos, watermarks, control-plane text, modern objects, duplicated people, or malformed anatomy.",
